From: ios-sapphire <research@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xnu: cpu 0390 — LDUMIN of the LSE emulation stores the minimum, not the operand

The kernel emulates the LSE atomics the iOS 16 userland uses on these ARMv8.0 cores (sleh.c sweet_emulate_lse ->
machine_routines_asm.s _sweet_lse_{b,h,w,x}). For UMAX (op 6) and UMIN (op 7) the macro compared the old value with
the operand, selected the UMAX result, then compared w1 with 6 to tell the two apart and selected the UMIN result on
the flags of that compare: w1 = 7 is not lower than 6, so LDUMIN stored the operand whatever the old value was.
UMIN now compares the old value with the operand again. Checked in EL0 on the phone with the macro copied as is
(dev-notes/investigacion/27, lsetest: 80 000 cases per operation and size): before, UMIN wrong in 40 049 of 80 000
and every other operation right; after, no case wrong.

---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
index 9faf940..a222d24 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
@@ -1378,10 +1378,15 @@ LEXT(_sweet_lse_\sfx)
 	cmp	\r\()12, \r\()13
 	csel	\r\()11, \r\()10, \r\()2, lt
 	b	5f
+	/*
+	 * sapphire 0390: UMAX (6) and UMIN (7) each select on the flags of their own compare of the old value with the
+	 * operand; UMIN selected on those of "cmp w1, #6" and stored the operand whatever the old value was.
+	 */
 27:	cmp	\r\()10, \r\()2
 	csel	\r\()11, \r\()10, \r\()2, hi
 	cmp	w1, #6
 	b.eq	5f
+	cmp	\r\()10, \r\()2
 	csel	\r\()11, \r\()10, \r\()2, lo
 5:	\stx	w9, \r\()11, [x0]
 	cbnz	w9, 1b
